# Locally computed (cabextract.org.uk does not publish a signed manifest
# alongside releases -- checked the release page directly at pin time).
#   sha256sum cabextract-1.11.tar.gz
#
# Both cabextract-1.11.tar.gz hashes below were computed from the tarball as
# served by the UPSTREAM site (www.cabextract.org.uk), then the mirror we
# actually download from was checked byte-for-byte against it -- see the
# CABEXTRACT_SITE comment in the .mk for why the fetch goes to Fedora's
# lookaside cache instead of upstream. (The COPYING hash at the bottom is
# unrelated to either host: it covers a file extracted from that tarball.)
sha256  b5546db1155e4c718ff3d4b278573604f30dd64c3c5bfd4657cd089b823a3ac6  cabextract-1.11.tar.gz
# sha512 is NOT redundant with the sha256 above: the lookaside URL embeds this
# exact value as a path segment (CABEXTRACT_SHA512 in the .mk), so listing it
# here makes Buildroot re-verify after download. A version bump that updates
# CABEXTRACT_SHA512 but not this line (or vice versa) then fails closed rather
# than quietly fetching a tarball nobody checked.
sha512  416bdc5a889c3986b2a5d6ecb8526a69f2d85c34f4856da43951271ff4f31013e4197c56ea5f6b05061b511b980d5a65cb34b9b859d3013c1dbcbb89d43114f9  cabextract-1.11.tar.gz
